{"judgments": [
  {
    "clause_id": "c001",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The sentence says coverage is provided by 'the Company designated by [an] \"X\" in the box below', yet only one company is typed and no marked box is legible, so the operative designation depends on a mark rather than words. The garbled '2 \"X\"' is a trivial transcription slip that does not itself change meaning.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It fits the rest of the certificate, which repeatedly refers to 'the Company' (Claims Made notice, acceptance clause) without contradiction, and the Zurich branding at the head confirms the identity.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.14,
    "prob_cat2": 0.07
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c002",
    "reasoning_cat1": "This is the classic claims-made-and-reported trigger: 'first be made and reported in writing to the Company during the \"Certificate Period\" or any applicable extended reporting period' invites argument over what counts as a 'claim', when it is 'first made', and what makes an ERP 'applicable', and the run-on punctuation joins the defense-costs sentence to it.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It depends on Item 5's 'Certificate Period', whose dates are illegible/garbled here, and its statement that 'Defense Costs are provided in addition to the Limits of Liability' must be squared with Item 4's limits and the incorporated Master Policy referenced in Items 7-8 and the acceptance clause.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.44,
    "prob_cat2": 0.33
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c003",
    "reasoning_cat1": "A bare name-and-address entry designating the Named Certificate Holder; it names one natural person with no ambiguous term to construe.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It is the referent for Item 4's per-holder limits, Item 5's local-time provision and the acceptance clause, and nothing in those provisions conflicts with naming Rosen individually, though whether his agency is also insured is left to Item 2.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.10,
    "prob_cat2": 0.14
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c004",
    "reasoning_cat1": "'Protective Life Insurance Company and Empire General and the Registered Representatives of ProEquities' is an open-ended and internally uneven list — whether every registered representative is an insured, and for what conduct, is not stated — and the entry is grammatically broken and truncated ('tac,').",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It must be read against Item 1's single Named Certificate Holder and Item 4's limits stated 'Each Named Certificate Holder' (which say nothing about additional insureds), and against Item 6's split deductible keyed to Protective Life/ProEquities products, leaving the additional insureds' coverage and share of limits unresolved.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.52,
    "prob_cat2": 0.36
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c005",
    "reasoning_cat1": "A producer name and mailing address only; there is no operative language capable of two readings.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "No other provision assigns the producer any duty, and notice under the claims-made clause runs to 'the Company', not the producer, so no conflict appears.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.06,
    "prob_cat2": 0.06
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c006",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The per-claim figure is rendered '$2,060,000,09' against a '$2,000,000.00' aggregate, a numerical/punctuation defect that could change the stated each-claim limit.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "Read with the header statement that 'Defense Costs are provided in addition to the Limits of Liability' and with the Master Policy referenced in Items 7-8, the interaction of the each-claim and aggregate limits per Named Certificate Holder (and whether additional insureds share them) is not fully settled here.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.27,
    "prob_cat2": 0.22
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c007",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The inception and expiry dates are illegible/impossible as written ('2/45/2007', '2/AS/2808') and the 'From 12:01 A.M.' text is transposed above the item label, so the period the policy actually runs cannot be read off the face of the clause.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "The Certificate Period is the operative trigger for the claims-made-and-reported requirement in the header notice, so any defect here directly affects whether a claim was timely made and reported.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.38,
    "prob_cat2": 0.30
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c008",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The split deductible sets a specific enumerated category ('products of Protective Life and ProEquities') against a residual catch-all ('all other covered products'), and 'covered products' is nowhere defined in the certificate, so the boundary between the $500 and $2,500 tiers — and what is a covered product at all — is open.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It presupposes a definition of covered products supplied only by the Master Policy incorporated through Items 7-8 and the acceptance clause, and it keys off the same entities named as Additional Insureds in Item 2, so the two entries must be harmonised.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.44,
    "prob_cat2": 0.31
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c009",
    "reasoning_cat1": "'Refer to Master Policy' is a pure cross-reference with no term to construe on its own.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It incorporates the Master Policy, which sits in tension with the closing clause's statement that 'this policy embodies all agreements' between the holder and the Company, though premium is unlikely to be the point of any dispute.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.08,
    "prob_cat2": 0.18
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c010",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The item promises 'Endorsements Effective at Inception' but lists none, deferring wholly to the Master Policy, so which endorsements (including any exclusions) attach at inception cannot be determined from the words used.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "This blank incorporation must be reconciled with the closing acceptance clause's integration language and with the certificate's own coverage terms (Items 4 and 6), since an unlisted endorsement could alter both.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.24,
    "prob_cat2": 0.31
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c011",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The clause is a merger/representations provision whose final sentence is cut off mid-phrase ('RELATING TO THIS'), and it simultaneously declares the certificate 'issued in accordance with the Master Policy' and that 'this policy embodies all agreements', a self-contained tension a court could be asked to resolve.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It sits directly against Items 7 and 8, which say 'Refer to Master Policy', and against the header's reference to the Master Policy's extended reporting period, so the extent to which the Master Policy's terms govern rather than the certificate alone is genuinely uncertain.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.37,
    "prob_cat2": 0.43
  }
]}

